From 607b6b5c5669246d37523011e10f1b55fdbf75ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:37:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: paint outside disc/circle/square markers with
 Chrome's geometry

Outside list markers were the font's bullet glyph placed flush against
the item, so with Liberation Sans the disc was smaller than Chrome's and
about 7px closer to the text at 17px. Chrome paints these three symbols
as shapes sized from the marker font's rounded ascent (diameter
ascent/3, offset 1px in and 3*(ascent - 2/3 ascent)/2 down from the text
top) and starts the marker box ascent*2/3 + 8px before the content edge
(Blink's ListMarker::InlineMarginsForOutside, RelativeSymbolMarkerRect
and ListMarkerPainter::PaintSymbol).

Outside markers whose content is `normal` and that have no
list-style-image now use that offset in OutsideMarker layout, and their
text fragment is painted as a filled circle, a 1px stroked circle or a
filled square, pixel-snapped like Blink. Measured against Chrome at
12-64px the shapes land within a pixel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
